RAN2/3 NR Source: NTT DOCOMO, INC. Decision: The document was revised to RP-172014. RP-172014 Updated work plan of RAN2/3 NR Source: NTT DOCOMO, INC. (Replaces RP-171715) Discussion: proposal: TSG-RAN provides the guidance for RAN2/3 in the next quarter to focus on the essential issues for EN-DC highlighted in this paper RAN chair: RAN2 already widely compliant to this? RAN2 chair: yes mainly, 3/4 NSA, 1/4 SA Qualcomm: this Tdoc seems to say focus on NSA so some details need more discussion LG: mainly fine with the Tdoc but some aspects to be discussed Samsung: most of Tdocs were not treated in RAN2, we should not stop SA discussions completely Nokia: supports Samsung statement that SA work shall not be stopped, e.g. important for slicing ZTE: supports Samsung and Nokia RAN chair: what information from RAN could help RAN2? RAN2 chair: some parts require further discussion so some guidance from RAN will help Interdigital: user plane needs to be completed for NSA and SA by Dec.17 Ericsson: RAN1 needs to be also aligned with the parts that have to be completed in RAN2 by Dec.17 RAN chair: we should have a separate Tdoc for RAN2 with the priorities ATT: wondering about "RAN2 works on RRC configuration required for this mobility type" RAN2 chair: this is a clarification for the bullet above RAN chair: could we do this on Monday evening in parallel to RAN1? seems so Samsung: if there are no mutual impacts, that's fine RAN3 part: NEC: whole split SRB on hold? RAN3 chair: RRC message transfer function does not take much time but clarifies that RAN3 is overloaded RAN chair: we need a Tdoc addressing the RAN3 NR WI priorities and also what to do with the SIs Deutsche Telekom: why is SON deprioritized? NTT DOCOMO: was deprioritized in RAN2 RAN chair: it seems for RAN3 we need to mainly clarify the handling of SI and this will be done in the revision of RP-172008 RAN3 chair: if RAN2 is downpriotizing something, then RAN3 will follow conclusion: RAN chair: RAN2 part will be discussed on Monday evening in breakout room Lilac with output in RP-172027 Decision: The document was noted. RP-172027 Updated work plan of RAN2 NR Source: RAN2 chairman (Intel) Discussion: Samsung: bullet 2 on slide 3 unclear RAN2 chair: you interpret "completed" stricter than I intended, not every detail needs to be completed; so better replace "completion" by "treatment" Orange: options 4 and 7: any priorities planned? RAN2 chair: many things applicable for option 2 and option 3 apply also to other options so we will still address them, things that are only relevant for option 4 will not be treated conclusion: "completion" will be changed into "treatment" Decision: The document was revised to RP-172068.

